  "notes": "Surface inventory derived 2026-08-23 directly from Chromium source: the three-line partial-interface IDL in html_image_element.idl (quoted verbatim on every page) and the dispatch/getter implementation in html_image_element.cc (StartImageReplacement, SetLayoutDisposition, ResetImageReplacement, replacedByUserAgent). The explainer (the ChromeStatus record's spec link — no WICG/W3C draft exists) supplies intent, non-goals, and privacy posture. Events verified to be plain Event instances (no payload, non-bubbling, non-cancelable, enqueued on the DOM-manipulation task source) — the pages state this from the implementation rather than inventing an event interface. No BCD/webstatus/MDN coverage exists; compat tables are labelled interim ChromeStatus data. Honest gaps: which Chrome UI features currently trigger replacement is not publicly enumerated (explainer non-goal), and the origin-trial registration status could not be machine-verified against the OT console (SPA) — the listing category is the authority for 'Origin trial'."
